The proof specification now compares the executed source program against an independent recursive oracle: uppercase/lowercase scoring, left-to-right selection, and strict replacement (hence first-on-ties). Seven end-to-end claims cover the prompt example, symbolic class names, ties, later winners, uncased characters, empty names, negative scores, and the singleton boundary. I’m doing the final clean scripted run now; its last command is the sole positive target proof.
